WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.740
This is the shop's Bay,

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:03.220
named after your shop,

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:06.260
so here it's Ridgeline Auto Repair Bay.

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:07.140
Under the name,

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.780
you can see how many cars are in

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:10.800
the shop, and how many updates went out

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:13.480
today. Every car sits in a column for

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:15.700
its stage, from checked in to ready for

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:18.260
pickup. The colored mark on each card shows

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:19.860
how long the car has been in the

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:21.820
shop, and you can pick the colors and

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:23.680
the days in Settings.

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:24.960
An urgency tag,

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:26.520
low, medium, or high,

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:30.020
flags a customer who needs their car back fast.

00:00:30.122 --> 00:00:31.922
Let's check in a new car.

00:00:31.922 --> 00:00:36.452
Sam Ortiz just dropped off his 2014 Mazda CX-5.

00:00:36.452 --> 00:00:39.332
We enter his name, and choose how to notify him:

00:00:39.332 --> 00:00:41.762
by text, by email, or both.

00:00:41.762 --> 00:00:43.562
Sam wants both.

00:00:43.562 --> 00:00:45.662
Then his cell number and email,

00:00:45.662 --> 00:00:48.002
the vehicle, and what he's hearing:

00:00:48.002 --> 00:00:50.792
a squealing belt on cold starts.

00:00:50.792 --> 00:00:54.662
This box confirms Sam agreed to receive updates.

00:00:54.662 --> 00:00:56.768
Then we check him in.

00:00:56.768 --> 00:00:57.668
And that's it.

00:00:57.668 --> 00:01:00.158
Sam was just notified that we have his car,

00:01:00.158 --> 00:01:01.808
with a link to follow along.

00:01:01.808 --> 00:01:03.938
That link is his own page for this car.

00:01:03.938 --> 00:01:06.128
No app, and no password.

00:01:06.128 --> 00:01:09.008
Every notification shows up here in the message thread,

00:01:09.008 --> 00:01:12.038
marked text or email, so the whole team can see what

00:01:12.038 --> 00:01:13.647
was sent and when.

00:01:13.647 --> 00:01:15.937
Now let's look at a car that's further along.

00:01:15.937 --> 00:01:19.647
Lena's Chevy Malibu came in with the AC blowing warm.

00:01:19.647 --> 00:01:20.967
The tech found the problem,

00:01:20.967 --> 00:01:22.767
so we'll build an estimate.

00:01:22.767 --> 00:01:26.487
As we type, Talk Shops suggests items the shop has saved,

00:01:26.487 --> 00:01:27.807
with their prices.

00:01:27.807 --> 00:01:29.787
We pick the AC recharge,

00:01:29.787 --> 00:01:31.617
for 189 dollars.

00:01:31.617 --> 00:01:34.077
Then the condenser, for 624.

00:01:34.077 --> 00:01:37.577
Anything new can be saved for next time with one checkbox.

00:01:38.011 --> 00:01:39.651
When the estimate is ready,

00:01:39.651 --> 00:01:41.411
we send it for approval.

00:01:41.411 --> 00:01:43.351
Talk Shops writes the message for you,

00:01:43.351 --> 00:01:45.411
with the total and the customer's link.

00:01:45.411 --> 00:01:47.531
You can change the wording if you like.

00:01:47.531 --> 00:01:49.292
Then we send it.

00:01:49.292 --> 00:01:51.892
Here's what Lena sees when she opens the link on her

00:01:51.892 --> 00:01:52.582
phone.

00:01:52.582 --> 00:01:54.592
Her car, where it's at in the process,

00:01:54.592 --> 00:01:55.552
and the estimate.

00:01:55.552 --> 00:01:58.702
She can approve or decline each repair on its own.

00:01:58.702 --> 00:02:00.772
Let's say she approves the recharge,

00:02:00.772 --> 00:02:02.962
but holds off on the condenser for now.

00:02:02.962 --> 00:02:04.702
She types her name to sign,

00:02:04.702 --> 00:02:06.172
and sends her decision.

00:02:06.172 --> 00:02:09.502
And every customer page links to the privacy policy at the

00:02:09.502 --> 00:02:12.010
bottom.

00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:15.100
Back at the shop, her answer shows up right away.

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:17.290
You can see exactly what she approved,

00:02:17.290 --> 00:02:19.010
and her signature with the time.

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:22.520
From here, you move the car along as the work happens.

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:23.630
In progress.

00:02:23.630 --> 00:02:24.920
Quality check.

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:26.840
Each step can notify the customer,

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:28.760
and you decide which ones go out.

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:31.400
And when it's done, ready for pickup.

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:34.900
The customer is notified with the total and your hours.
